From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 9 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: use duelist helpers in operations.cpp

Sites changed (same behaviour with 2 duelists):
- 17 lines of 1 - x became opponent_of(x): draw confirm player, damage reflect (2), unique check toggle (3), control swap (1 line, 2 uses), trap monster adjust (2), hint timing, spsummon counter, move player toggle, reason player toggle, QuickEffect player, dice messages (2). All x are duelist indexes or go into a uint8_t.
- 1 turn-player-first loop (trap monster adjust) now counts n_duelists and steps with next_in_turn_order.
- 3 local arrays of size 2 became MAX_DUELISTS: decktop, s (xyz material deck size), spsummon_once_set. Two new local arrays d and s replace d0/d1/s0/s1 in send_to.
- Pairs became loops over n_duelists in the order 0 then 1: xyz deck top messages, writetopcard, deck top messages in send_to, check_decktop_visibility reset and check, shuffle hand and deck checks (two loops, hand first), spsummon_once_map, card spsummon counters reset, priorities reset.

The order of messages, events and shuffles stays the same, because every loop runs 0 then 1 with n_duelists == 2.

Left unchanged: 3 uses of 1 - sumplayer or 1 - setplayer (decision needed), the ControlAdjust pair logic, 40 PLAYER_NONE uses (phase 2), and non player sites. See unchanged-sites.md.
